                <pb facs="0683" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2357: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract–Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-04T14:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1922—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 5—9:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>45. I was requested by the President to advise Department concerning political
                    difficulties of Honduras and Nicaragua. He is reliably informed that Francisco
                    Martinez Funes is at present in Esteli and has 300 troops equipped to make an
                    invasion of Honduras. He requests that representations be made by the Department
                    to Nicaragua that Funes be captured. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
